## 1. Introduction: The Recurrent Error

The historical pattern of idol worship is not a religious anomaly—it is a *structural error* that repeats across cultures, eras, and domains. It is the act of treating human creations (artifacts) as if they were natural or divine (facts). This error is the root of systemic collapse, from the fall of empires to the current crisis of the global paradigm.

The polymath tradition, from Imhotep in 27th century BC Egypt  to the present, has sought to transcend disciplinary boundaries and identify the underlying structures of error. This paper continues that tradition.

